# A111603

Consider the array T(n, m) where the n-th row is the sequence of integer coefficients of A(x), where 1<=a(n)<=n, such that A(x)^(1/n) consists entirely of integer coefficients and where m is the (m+1)-th coefficient. This is the antidiagonal read from upper right to lower left.

The 101 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

